-- ported from tests/cases/compiler/continueNotInIterationStatement2.ts
-- dropped: @target: es2015 directive (tlua defaults to latest target)
-- dropped: emit coverage (noEmit) -- the `continue` is rejected for crossing a function
-- boundary, so the recovered tree emits a `continue` inside `f`, which has no enclosing
-- loop and is invalid Lua.


while true do
>true : true

    function f()
>f : () => void

        continue
    end
end

